# Tasks: Phase 1 Bug Fixes & Stability

**Input**: Design documents from `speckit.specify` and `speckit.plan`
**Target Branch**: `phase1-bug-fixes` (`/home/pplupo/repos/webui2`)
**Prerequisites**: speckit.plan (required), speckit.specify (required)

## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files/modules, no direct dependencies)
- **[Story]**: Target bug fix / user story (US1: #72 URL Crash, US2: #89 Completed Projects, US3: #59 CLI Data Robustness, US4: #90 Mobile Input Offset)

---

## Phase 1: Setup & Foundational Prerequisites

**Purpose**: Baseline verification of branch and component entry points

- [x] T001 Verify clean test environment and target files in `frontend/` and `backend/`.

---

## Phase 2: User Story 1 - Fix URL Parsing Crash on Double Colons (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Prevent list view crashes caused by invalid URL parsing when task titles contain double colons (`::`) or malformed strings (#72).
**Independent Test**: Load tasks with descriptions containing `Doug:: double-check re: Thursday meeting`, `test::value`, and `http://example.com`; verify table and Kanban render smoothly and pagination functions without exceptions.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T002 [P] [US1] Create defensive URL validation and sanitization utility in `frontend/utils/linkify.ts` matching explicit schemes (`http://`, `https://`, `ftp://`) and `www.*` domains while rejecting pseudo-schemes like `Doug::`.
- [x] T003 [US1] Update `linkify` implementation in `frontend/components/TaskList.vue` to use the defensive utility with fallback to plain text.
- [x] T004 [US1] Update `linkify` implementation in `frontend/components/KanbanCard.vue` to use the defensive utility with fallback to plain text.

---

## Phase 3: User Story 2 - Completed Projects Separation & Setting Toggle (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Place 100% completed projects below a divider in the project selector and allow hiding them completely via a user setting, default hidden (#89).
**Independent Test**: Create a project where all tasks are completed/deleted. Verify it is hidden by default in the project selector. Uncheck "Hide completed projects" in SettingsDialog and verify the completed project appears at the bottom under a divider.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T005 [P] [US2] Update Vuex store in `frontend/store/index.ts` to add getters for `activeProjects` (projects with at least one pending/waiting task) and `completedProjects` (projects where all tasks are completed or deleted).
- [x] T006 [P] [US2] Add `hideCompletedProjects: true` state, mutation, and `localStorage` persistence in `frontend/store/index.ts`.
- [x] T007 [US2] Add "Hide completed projects" checkbox in `frontend/components/SettingsDialog.vue`.
- [x] T008 [US2] Update `projectOptions` computed property in `frontend/pages/index.vue` to render active projects, and append divider + completed projects when `hideCompletedProjects` is false.

---

## Phase 4: User Story 3 - Theme Include & CLI Data Fetching Robustness (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: Ensure Taskwarrior CLI output formatting and color themes never corrupt backend JSON data fetching (#59).
**Independent Test**: Run queries with theme includes in `.taskrc` or with color forcing; verify backend parses task list cleanly into JSON without formatting artifacts.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T009 [P] [US3] Update `backend/src/taskwarrior.ts` to enforce `rc._forcecolor=off` and `rc.defaultwidth=0` on Taskwarrior invocations.
- [x] T010 [US3] Add robust error handling around `taskwarrior.load()` in `backend/src/tasks.ts` to report clean structured error messages if `.taskrc` configuration errors occur.

---

## Phase 5: User Story 4 - Prevent Mobile (iOS) Input Offset (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: Eliminate input field coordinate and cursor offset desynchronization during validation errors on mobile devices (#90).
**Independent Test**: On a mobile/narrow viewport emulation, trigger a validation error on due date in TaskDialog; verify the cursor remains properly aligned inside the text field without coordinate detachment.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T011 [US4] Update text field inputs in `frontend/components/TaskDialog.vue` with `hide-details="auto"` and stable container sizing to prevent layout shift on validation error display.

---

## Phase 6: Polish & Cross-Cutting Verification

**Purpose**: End-to-end integration and smoke verification across all fixed components

- [x] T012 Run frontend linter and typecheck (`npm run lint` / `npm run build` or equivalent).
- [x] T013 Verify complete Phase 1 bug fix user journeys across Table, Kanban, and Dialogs.

